  s0: Input waits for the owner (Claude busy)
  s1: Input waits for the owner (Claude idle)
  s2: Input held for a later wake (Claude idle)
  s3: Pasted, no row yet
  s4: Input kept, person asked to send again
  s5: Input held for a later wake (Claude busy)
  s6: Claude queued it behind the running turn
  s7: Opened its own turn
  s8: Opened its own turn, nobody answers it
  s9: Answer posted
  [*] --> s0
  [*] --> s1
  s0 --> s3: the owner pastes into the AgentDesk turn [refused when the transcript is idle, main]
  s1 --> s2: the owner submits to an idle pane
  s1 --> s4: the owner pastes into the AgentDesk turn [refused when the transcript is idle, main]
  s2 --> s5: a person starts a turn at the terminal
  s3 --> s6: Claude writes an enqueue row
  s5 --> s2: the turn ends
  s6 --> s7: the turn ends
  s7 --> s8: the relay reads the input's row
  s8 --> s9: the turn ends
